<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 44,651 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 44,651 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 44,651 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 34,206 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     March 24</p>
<p>    Export cargo		15,932	18,929</p>
<p>    Import cargo		28,719	15,277</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, 10 are expected to sail and 11 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Soyoil		   18,000	 P.B. Courage	 26/3</p>
<p>Gas oil		  25,000	 San Sebastian	26/3</p>
<p>High speed diesel    78,750	 Chesapeak City     27/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,200	 Global Juno	  28/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
